WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.640
<i>Monsters threaten human life.</i>

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.690
<i>They are opposed by brave adventurers!</i>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.550
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.490
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.390
my journey continues!

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.350
My Healer!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:02:00.340
<b>This episode features even more female guest characters hot on the heels...</b>

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.540
We found the crystal ball, but...

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.340
this sure isn't my sword.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.780
Is it a goddess statue?

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.610
It does appear that way.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.090
And my crystal ball is in pieces.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.070
Looks like you hit it right in the head.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:08.990
What are you going to do?

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.970
You think it's going to lead 
to divine retribution?

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.730
I could hardly be a holy woman if I 
was afraid of divine retribution.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.740
I think that's exactly something 
a holy woman shouldn't say.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.170
Who goes there?!

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.000
A monster?

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:25.860
Were you the ones who broke my seal?

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.160
A seal?

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.390
You have my gratitude, truly...

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.000
I can at last resume my reign 
of terror over humanity!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.460
Wretched monster!

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:38.690
What now?!

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.220
You heard what she said.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:41.570
Let's beat her!

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.550
It does seem like it would be in the 
interest of keeping the peace...

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.940
Actually, her hoity-toity 
phrasing just pisses me off.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:47.460
So it's all about you?!

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:47.940
Yes.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.750
But I don't have my sword!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.030
But look!

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:55.490
She was sealed away in 
that tiny little hole.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:57.440
She's probably small and weak!

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.450
Just step on her and it's a done deal!

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.180
You think I can handle it?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.660
If it doesn't work, 
I'll hit her with a tieshankao!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:05.500
Great!

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.380
For the sake of world peace, 
I will defeat you!

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.430
Show yourself!

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.460
We'll give you a sock to 
that smug mouth of yours!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.410
Oh? Feeling suicidal, are we?

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:16.990
She's over there, I think.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:17.750
Right.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.150
Excellent timing.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:22.630
I need a little exercise to wake 
me up after a long sleep...

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:25.020
We'll face you! Just show yourself!

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.470
How bold you are.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.930
You truly believe you can defeat me?

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.670
Now, let us battle!

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:39.640
What the hell?!

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:40.710
She's not small at all!

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:42.440
What are you doing?

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.880
Alvin-san, be careful!

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:45.830
She's a Medusa!

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.560
M-Medusa?!

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.200
If you look into her eyes, 
she'll turn you to stone!

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.490
I know that!

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.930
Listen to me! You must not look, 
no matter what happens!

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.090
I said I know!

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.960
You must not! Ever!

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.330
Never, ever, ever!

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.250
Stop saying that!

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.140
Seriously, don't do it, okay?

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:12.150
Glance!

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.630
You looked!

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:14.270
Shu-wah!

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.370
Oh, cra—

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:22.960
Alvin-san!

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.440
Wow, how stupid is he?

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.310
It's all my fault...

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:29.800
I'm not sure I'd say that.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.710
I would say it's his fault.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:35.770
No, I should've realized 
that if I kept warning him,

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.240
he'd assume it was a joke setup, 
and end up looking!

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.220
The way your mind works is a mystery to me.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:45.010
But never you mind!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.480
I'll get you, too!

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.850
But look at you, Alvin-san! 
This is just too on the nose.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.370
It breaks my heart.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.470
You look like one of those heavy stones—

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.050
I'm not a paperweight!

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.520
I didn't call you a paperweight.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.210
You were about t—

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:00.560
Yes?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.140
Just let me finish!

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.520
How...

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.830
How did you shake off my petrification?

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.550
Huh? Hey, good question!

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.480
Curse you!

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:09.770
One more time!

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.120
I won't make the same mistake twice!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.120
Aw, c'mon! You gotta look at me!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.900
What kind of idiot would look, 
knowing it would turn him to stone?!

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.620
Alvin-san!

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.380
Look! You have to look!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.690
Alvin-san, you made her cry!

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.590
You big meanie!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.660
You really don't have to cry—

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.720
Fool! Shu-wah!

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.550
Alvin-san!

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:34.360
Goodness me...

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.840
Did I getcha this time?!

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.870
What's wrong with you?

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:38.600
Come on...

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.100
Just shake off the petrification 
like last time!

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.670
Just do it again!

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.490
You know, the "pop" thing!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.740
C'mon, please!

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:48.990
Please? Please?

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.300
Alvin-san!

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.620
Quit enjoying this!

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.580
Yikes!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:56.900
For real, what's going on here?!

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.940
Why? Why won't it work?

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.330
My specialty... My identity...

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.670
More crocodile tears, huh?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.100
But I won't be fooled again!

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.590
It's painful for anyone to have 
their identity denied to them.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.690
Just like Alvin-san...

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:19.370
You wouldn't have anything left if 
you took off that armor, right?

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.990
Uh, I'd still have my body!

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.790
Medusa-san.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.480
You can't let a small setback 
like this get you down.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:30.350
You've just been sealed away so long, 
you haven't recovered all your power yet.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:32.370
Really?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.960
Yes, really.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.830
Come on. Chin up! 
Take pride in yourself!

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.260
You are a Medusa, a legendary monster!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:43.120
The way this is going...

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.880
That's right...

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.590
You're exactly right.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.100
I'll keep trying!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:53.760
Shu-wah!

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.320
<i>Yeah, knew it!</i>

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.590
Wow.

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:05.310
So you can't do the petrification 
without the "shu-wah," huh?

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.410
Yeah.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.470
I wouldn't have much of a social life

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:10.570
if I could petrify people just 
by looking at them, right?

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.060
You have a social life?

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:13.640
Like this?

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.740
More like jazz hands.

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:16.370
They're actually getting along.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.270
Alvin-san!

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.680
What the heck?!

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.660
I thought I sensed an evil presence here.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:26.750
Tch!

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.910
You're the woodland spirit...

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.130
Dryad!

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.400
I knew it would be you, Medusa!

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:39.530
I am this forest's guardian.

00:07:39.530 --> 00:07:44.210
Human, releasing the Medusa 
is a terribly grave crime.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.140
Hang on a minute!

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:46.710
I'm not the one who released the seal—

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.250
Excuses, excuses!

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:49.910
Stay out of this, true culprit!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.520
I found this near the destroyed statue.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.770
Does it belong to you two?

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:57.870
My crystal ball!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.940
She admits it!

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.660
Pay me back for that!

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.880
Harrumph!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.370
You're going to <i>sue</i> a monster?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:04.810
I see.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.620
So you destroyed the statue seal.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.430
Are you aware of what you've done?

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.880
Have I done something again?

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:19.350
Long ago, Medusa terrorized 
countless towns and villages.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.660
You have unleashed a truly 
terrifying monster!

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.560
Wow, sounds like you had quite a career!

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:30.970
Ah, it's easy when you're young.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.040
Seems like you've softened up since then.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.410
It does appear she's lost 
a great deal of power.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.160
Which means this is my best chance.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.930
I entreat you to take responsibility 
and defeat Medusa!

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.430
She means <i>you</i>!

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.280
Don't look at me!

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.690
At least release Alvin-san first!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.560
It's so hard to see him like this.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:54.810
Carla...

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:55.900
Oh?

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:01.170
It pains you to see a comrade in 
a humiliating position, you mean?

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:03.530
But if you want him freed, 
defeat Medusa first.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.680
Oh, good grief.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.380
You've misunderstood me.

00:09:07.930 --> 00:09:12.580
What I mean is, no one wants to see a 
thirty-something man engaged in bondage!

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.210
Don't call it bondage!

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.690
Now I'm even more embarrassed!

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.890
Such things are the exclusive purview 
of beautiful maidens such as myself.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:22.580
Feel free to swap in, then! 
We'd all like to see it!

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.220
Busted for sexual harassment!

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.680
Are you mocking me?

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.370
Look, you're making the dryad angry! 
Infuriated, even!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:31.240
A thirty-something man engaged in bondage...

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:32.860
is totally hot!

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:33.800
Dryad-san?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.600
Oh, please!

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.100
"But only if he's hot," right?

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:39.510
What are you guys talking about?

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:43.990
Actually, I find it even more stimulating 
when the man is <i>un</i>attractive!

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:44.690
Take that!

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:46.760
Do we need to know all this about you?!

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.800
Calm down, both of you!

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:50.670
Medusa is the only sane one here!

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.350
Pure hell.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:55.570
I like it best when they're underage!

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:58.620
Can we not bring shotacon into this?!

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.010
Alvin-san doesn't qualify as any 
of those, so please release him!

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:06.870
We can't know that until 
we see his real face.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.110
If he's a baby-face, I might still be down!

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.510
These freaks...

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.340
Then let's find our answer.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:15.290
H-Hey, cut it out!

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.830
What's with you girls?

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:19.330
Weren't we talking about defeating Medusa?

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:21.040
Why is this happening?!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.560
Hey. Don't go silent now.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.320
At least say what you think of how I look!

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.650
Pathetic.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.360
Utterly lacking in distinction.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.440
I'll forget it within two hours.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.080
Well, so sorry to disappoint!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.950
I'm sorry. It was wrong of me.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.700
I shouldn't have tried to make 
you defeat the evil Medusa.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.730
Not at all.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:55.990
I share a bit of fault for 
how things went down...

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.470
About 1% or so.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:02.120
If you'd mentioned that earlier, I could've 
made some preparations myself...

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.590
I didn't realize he'd be this weak.

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:08.140
When I heard that he'd 
resisted your stone gaze,

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.860
I thought he might be a 
match for you, but...

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:16.670
And I'm not feeling my best, so I'd 
buckled in for a tough battle...

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:17.860
At least let me get a word in!

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.260
Alvin-san.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.600
The loser doesn't get an opinion.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:23.660
Know your place.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.980
Lay off, damn it!

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.250
Listen to me.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.960
I know I'm really weak, okay?

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:28.860
Yes, he is!

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.910
But despite appearances,

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.140
I honestly do daily muscle 
training and sword practice!

00:11:34.140 --> 00:11:35.260
What else?

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:37.250
But I didn't stand a chance this time.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:38.830
Do you know why that is?

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.260
Yes? One, two...

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.370
Why is that?!

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.260
Just shut up!

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:43.780
There's only one reason!

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.730
Because I don't have my sword right now!

00:11:48.280 --> 00:11:50.630
<i>Now</i> talk, damn it!

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:53.140
Seems to me like the sword is 
the least of his problems.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.970
Why in the world doesn't 
he have a sword, anyway?

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:55.780
Isn't he a warrior?

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:58.800
He's not just a shady character 
in a tin-plated suit?

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:02.190
Is there a funnier joke 
than the tin-plated thing?

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:03.910
I hear you! Especially you, Carla!

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.650
If you need a sword, I know of one.

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:10.660
A sacred sword stuck in a 
pedestal deep in the forest.

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:12.360
A sacred sword?

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:18.260
Many adventurers have attempted 
to draw the sword...

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.270
but none of them have succeeded.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:25.170
But you two, who were present 
for Medusa's unsealing...

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:27.940
Though we were the ones who 
started the whole mess...

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:32.410
The time, indeed, may have come for 
the sacred sword to be drawn!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:33.810
There it is!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:37.920
Is that...

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.860
the legendary...

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.200
sacred sword?!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.330
Why's it stuck in that way?!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:51.220
Go on! Pull it out!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.420
Like hell!

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.720
Isn't the hilt supposed to 
be the exposed part?!

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.790
Alvin... can you hear me?

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:02.100
Alvin... can you hear my voice?

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.220
What the...

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.130
A voice!

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:05.830
Can it be...

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:07.420
I am the sacred sword.

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:09.430
Is it really a sacred sword?!

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.550
Hero Alvin.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:15.380
I have awaited your arrival!

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:17.070
I'm a hero?

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:17.930
Are you kidding me?!

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:21.000
Yes. You are the chosen hero.

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.670
The hero, chosen by random lottery...

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.630
Random lottery?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.450
Now, extract me—

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:28.900
What?

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:32.340
The voice is on a bit of a lag...

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.200
Screw that!

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.530
That was your voice, damn it!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:38.110
I can't believe I got my hopes up for that!

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:40.080
I'm sorry. Vewwy sowwy.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.140
I thought you deserved 
a nice dream for once.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.580
It's more like a nightmare I 
can't wait to wake up from!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.520
Anyway, let's see if you 
can pull out the sword!

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.610
Yeah! Yeah!

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:52.590
I'd doubt it'll work, 
but I might as well try...

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.320
Looks pretty tough, though...

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:57.740
I guess I'll have to grab it by the blade.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.020
What's the matter?

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.680
I think it's loose.

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.580
I'm sure he's imagining it.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.650
Most likely his imagination.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:09.890
Are you deluding yourself?

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.360
You guys!

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.910
Darn it...

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.300
I'll just have to force it out!

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:25.730
Is he really the chosen one?

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:27.580
When did he apply for that?!

00:14:27.580 --> 00:14:30.860
I didn't apply for anything!

00:14:32.070 --> 00:14:32.990
He pulled it out!

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:35.170
Wait, he really is the chosen one?!

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:36.740
No! Look closely!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.100
<b>Dud</b>

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.740
It was a dud draw.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.740
What in the world does that mean?!

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.870
W-Well, good for you!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.570
You got a sacred sword!

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:53.610
A dud one, sure!

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.150
I bet you're thinking it's 
perfect for me, huh?

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:58.040
Go ahead and laugh, if you want!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:59.620
Really? Can I?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.110
Thank you so much!

00:15:01.800 --> 00:15:03.370
Never mind, never laugh again!

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:05.240
But my smile is my best trait!

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:06.100
So mean!

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:08.010
You might wanna rethink that one!

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:11.610
If you took away my smile, 
what else would I have?

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.840
Unpleasantness.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.140
Look at you, pouting.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.880
Just cheer up already!

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:21.030
You already have a jackpot, you know...

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:23.030
The jackpot known as Carla.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:23.830
Jackpot!

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:24.730
Gosh, I'm blushing.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:27.410
More like a crackpot!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.950
But now that you have a sword,

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.880
show me the fruits of this 
daily training of yours!

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:36.720
Not like one little sword is gonna 
make a difference against me!

00:15:37.930 --> 00:15:39.780
She's mocking you, Alvin-san!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:41.960
I believe in you!

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:45.200
I believe that your daily training 
will be a drop in the bucket!

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.380
You realize you're making things 
worse right now, right?

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:49.800
No need to be worried!

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.400
I will support you!

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.170
Now I'm even more worried!

00:15:53.570 --> 00:15:55.370
Two on one, eh?

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.060
A perfectly fine handicap for me!

00:15:57.250 --> 00:15:59.700
I'm the one with a handicap here!

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.750
Look at this guy!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.680
I can hear you, damn it!

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:06.540
Say what you want about me, but all 
you do is sit on the back lines!

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.190
Say that all you like, 
but you're the one who—

00:16:08.420 --> 00:16:10.360
Here we go again!

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:12.600
I can't tell if they are 
a good pairing or not.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:15.150
What spell shall I use this time?

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.810
Drumroll...

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:17.500
Ta-da!

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:22.130
A defense-enhancing spell!

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:24.690
Everything you do is unpleasant!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.460
With one cast of this spell...

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.150
Behold!

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.560
Behold what?

00:16:30.560 --> 00:16:32.480
All you did was clap your hands—

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:35.410
Wait... what are you doing?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.240
What are you doing—

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:45.050
See? It didn't hurt at all, right?

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:47.640
It certainly dealt psychological damage!

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:51.380
But there was no <i>physical</i> damage, was there?

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.770
That's because of my spell.

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:56.040
It's true that it didn't hurt much at all...

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:59.330
Perhaps she was unconsciously 
taking it easy on her comrade?

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.770
Allow me to take over!

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.910
Why?

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.300
Just remove your armor and 
get down on all fours!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:08.420
Oh, me next! I wanna do it next!

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.800
But why should I—

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.310
Hurry!

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.310
I'm not a chair, damn it!

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:18.560
Let us begin!

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.230
One more time!

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:21.510
It's not over yet!

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:22.980
Take that!

00:17:23.470 --> 00:17:26.470
You like that? Tell me you love it!

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.470
Dryad-san, stop!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.700
Well? Any damage?

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:34.110
Only to your image, I think!

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:37.480
It does appear he didn't feel anything.

00:17:37.480 --> 00:17:38.420
What a disappointment.

00:17:38.420 --> 00:17:40.570
Could you not say stuff that 
could be taken the wrong way?

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:42.000
Now it's my turn!

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:45.360
But this is pretty cool! 
It doesn't hurt at all!

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:46.460
Right?

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.100
Look at you! 
You actually cast a proper spell!

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.090
Sexual harassment...

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.330
If not for that part...

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.560
The next! Me! My turn!

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:56.330
I'm not a dang punching bag!

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:57.570
Fine.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:00.390
Thanks to Carla, I might just 
come out well in this match!

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.520
<i>And</i> I have a sword!

00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:03.960
But you should probably hurry.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:08.190
When the spell ends, you'll feel the 
previously negated damage twice as hard!

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:12.100
Or was that ten times as hard?

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.470
My turn!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:25.960
Delicious!

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:28.220
Yeah, not bad at all!

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:30.460
I'm pleased that you like it.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:34.330
I made the cake out of the 
forest's best fruits.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:37.870
You're pretty good at the girl stuff, 
despite all the weird fetishes.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.710
You are quite the irritating, little reptile.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:42.740
The taste puts me in mind of a temple 
built to restore the clean air

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:46.370
of a cursed ground plagued 
by storms of miasma.

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:51.940
Specifically, the flower that 
grows beside the wind god there.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.920
Specifically, the caterpillars 
that feed on the flower.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.860
I don't believe that's a compliment.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:18:59.700
And how is Alvin-san feeling?

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.080
He'll wake up soon.

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:06.260
I drew him a special healing magic circle.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.680
Thank you for letting us 
use your room, Dryad-san.

00:19:12.680 --> 00:19:13.370
Think nothing of it!

00:19:13.370 --> 00:19:14.920
Fate has brought us together, after all.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:19.540
It is a weird turn of fate that we're ending 
up in this kind of weird girls' get-together...

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:24.440
Speaking of fate, how'd you end up 
in a party with that guy, Carla?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:30.170
This is kinda blunt, but what do you have to 
gain partying up with a warrior that weak?

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.810
I mean, I can tell he's a decent dude...

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:36.380
but as party members go, 
he seems like a bit of a load.

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:39.370
I'm impressed he's even still alive.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.720
Oh, sorry!

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:44.250
I wasn't trying to badmouth your partner...

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:47.340
Could I have another piece of cake?

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:48.760
C-Certainly!

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:51.070
I understand how you feel, of course.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:55.640
But he has quite a number of good points

00:19:55.640 --> 00:19:57.840
as befits his title of 
"Weakest Loser Master King."

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:00.840
I don't think I'd want traits 
befitting that title...

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:03.140
For instance...

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.720
You're stuck already?

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:08.690
Patheticness!

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:09.800
That's an insult.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:10.580
Wretchedness!

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:11.230
So is that.

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:12.030
Suckiness!

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:13.100
Seriously?!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:17.690
Um... but it's more than that.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.610
Maybe keep the next one to yourself.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:23.000
Being with him is fun.

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.890
What are we talking about?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.260
You scared me... not a bit!

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:34.060
Not a tiny little bit!

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.140
That was a hell of a reaction.

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:40.010
Did you hear what we were saying?

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:42.760
No, all I heard was that you were talking.

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:45.160
We were talking about you!

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.520
About me?

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:49.030
Nothing good, I'm sure.

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:51.720
She's saying I'm pathetic and 
wretched and sucky, I'll bet.

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.090
Three for three!

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:55.600
B-But Carla-chan said you were—

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.310
You scared me!

00:20:58.310 --> 00:20:59.820
Where did that come from?

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:03.770
I just saw a meteorite!

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.190
Indoors?

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:07.320
Sorry, could you say that again?

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.200
Oh, shut up!

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:10.910
Wow! Shooting star!

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.670
You can change what you call it, 
but we're still indoors!

00:21:13.670 --> 00:21:15.090
What in the world is wrong with you?

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:17.690
Is it really something 
that bad for me to hear?

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:18.740
It's not like that.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:20.420
Then, shut up!

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.750
Now, what were you talking about?

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:26.090
W-Well—

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:29.620
I'm sorry. I completely forgot!

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:32.310
You forgot what we were just talking about?

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.680
I remember, though!

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:35.490
Please don't!

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:36.680
Listen, Alvin!

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.320
Carla said that being with you was—

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:41.690
Achoo!

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:46.400
Drat! I just sneezed!

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.760
Who unleashes a tieshankao 
when they sneeze?!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>Try again in 
ten years' time!</b>

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.610 --> 00:23:27.150
Next episode's title is...

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:28.000
Dryad!

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:29.560
Me, too! Me, too! Me, too!

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:30.260
Let me do it, too!

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:32.050
Don't interrupt, Medusa!

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:34.340
Just sit there and do your "Shu-wah!"

00:23:34.340 --> 00:23:36.050
Aw, no way! No way!

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:37.680
I wanna do it, too!

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:37.680
You truly are annoying!

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>"In the second half of this episode, we enter the "What Story Is This?" 
arc (though actually it's just the next two episodes) so let me explain
once again for people not in the know that "What Story Is This?" is the
webcomic version of the story that would eventually be published as
"Don't Hurt Me, My Healer," so this arc isn't included in the printed
comic but you should still be able to read it so go ahead and do that if
you like but at the same time there's also a thankless role in the first
half so I'll ask you to keep an eye on that because it's going to
be clear it's an important event if you keep
watching and that's the deal with episode 10."</b>

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.560
Let me try it!
